          <select id="hs-ind">{Object.entries(INDUSTRIES).map(([k, v]) => <option value={k} selected={k === 'other'}>{v.label}</option>)}</select>
          <p class="note" data-o="note">{r.note}</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>Turnover <b data-o="turn">{(r.turnoverRate * 100).toFixed(1)}%</b></span><span>Absence <b data-o="abs">{r.absenceDays.toFixed(1)} days</b></span><span>Presenteeism <b data-o="pres">{Math.round(r.presRate * 100)}%</b></span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="in">
          <div class="in-row"><label for="hs-sal">Average salary</label><small>optional</small></div>
          <div class="money"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span><input type="text" id="hs-sal" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" value={S0} /></div>
          <p class="note">Defaults to a sensible blended figure if you skip it.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">Built on Gallup engagement data, SHRM turnover benchmarks and current Australian psychosocial safety regulation. Indicative for a conversation, not a substitute for one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="outs">
        <div class="tile">
          <span class="eyebrow">The human picture</span>
          <p class="body">Behind every percentage point is a person. Of your <b data-o="n">{num(N0)}</b> people, today the picture looks roughly like this.</p>
          <div class="cells">
            <div class="cell"><b data-o="c1">{num(r.disengaging)}</b><small data-o="p1">{pct(r.disengaging, N0)}</small><h4>Quietly disengaging</h4><span>Showing up. Holding back.</span></div>
            <div class="cell"><b data-o="c2">{num(r.heading)}</b><small data-o="p2">{pct(r.heading, N0)}</small><h4>Heading toward burnout</h4><span>Sleep, focus, mood slipping.</span></div>
            <div class="cell hot"><b data-o="c3">{num(r.burnout)}</b><small data-o="p3">{pct(r.burnout, N0)}</small><h4>Already in burnout</h4><span>Exhausted, often hiding it.</span></div>
            <div class="cell hot"><b data-o="c4">{num(r.crisis)}</b><small data-o="p4">{pct(r.crisis, N0)}</small><h4>In genuine crisis</h4><span>Where harm and liability start.</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="fine">Gallup 2024 · Deloitte AU Mental Health &amp; Employers 2024 · Black Dog Institute.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tile">
          <div class="cost-hd">
            <div>
              <span class="eyebrow">Annual cost to you</span>
              <p class="body">Around <b class="hot-t" data-o="hid">{r.hiddenPct}%</b> of this never reaches the dashboard. It compounds quietly until it surfaces.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cost-total"><b data-o="total">{aud(r.total)}</b><small>per year, indicative</small></div>
          </div>
          <div class="buckets">
            <div class="bucket">
              <span class="b-k">Visible</span><span class="b-t">In the books</span>
              <p><span>Absenteeism</span><b data-o="absc">{aud(r.absenteeism)}</b></p>
              <p><span>Turnover and replacement</span><b data-o="turnc">{aud(r.turnover)}</b></p>
              <p class="sub"><span>Subtotal</span><b data-o="vis">{aud(r.visible)}</b></p>
            </div>
            <div class="bucket hidden-b">
              <span class="b-k">Hidden</span><span class="b-t">Off the dashboard</span>
              <p><span>Presenteeism and lost focus</span><b data-o="presc">{aud(r.presenteeism)}</b></p>
              <p class="sub"><span>Subtotal</span><b data-o="presc">{aud(r.presenteeism)}</b></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tile risk">
          <p class="risk-hd"><span class="eyebrow">Regulatory exposure · Victoria</span><span class="risk-pill" data-o="risk">{r.risk}</span></p>
          <p class="risk-line"><span data-o="crisis-n">{num(r.crisis)} {r.crisis === 1 ? 'person' : 'people'}</span> in crisis is <span class="hot-t" data-o="claims">{claimText(r.claims)}</span></p>
          <p class="range-out"><b data-o="low">{aud(r.low)}</b><span>to</span><b data-o="high">{aud(r.high)}</b></p>
          <p class="body">Anchored to <i>WorkSafe Victoria v Court Services Victoria</i>, 2023: AU$379,157 for a single psychosocial safety breach. Applied to your at-risk group at an 8% claim conversion rate.</p>
          <p class="body" style="font-size:15px">Since 1 December 2025, Victoria’s amended OHS Regulations make managing psychosocial hazards an explicit legal duty. Maximum body-corporate penalties reach AU$3.85M per offence. Equivalent duties now apply in NSW, QLD, WA, SA and the UK.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="calc-end">This is the cost of not having a human strategy.<br /><span>Here is how we build one.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How I can help -->
